<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<catalogue xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema" id="4b64-b0f5-2138-7dbe" name="Homebrew - Grey Knights" revision="53" battleScribeVersion="2.03" library="false" gameSystemId="28d4-bd2e-4858-ece6" gameSystemRevision="130" type="catalogue" authorName="Isaac">
  <publications>
    <publication id="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f" name="Grey Knights for The Horus Heresy 2.0 — Homebrew Conversion" shortName="HB - Grey Knights" />
  </publications>
  <selectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grey Knights" hidden="false" id="fa33-cf16-cc44-f9c7" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <modifiers>
        <modifier type="set" field="7942-3fc4-1d05-bcf9" value="0">
          <conditions>
            <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="f9c0-0c5a-3e24-58c7" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" shared="true" id="518b-5131-62ea-5937" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" shared="true" id="7942-3fc4-1d05-bcf9" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Psychic Ward" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="a6a8-1a04-a436-a846">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Shooting phase). Trigger: a Grey Knights unit is selected as the target of a Shooting Attack or a psychic weapon. Before the attack is resolved, the unit casts Sanctuary on itself (taking a Psychic check as normal).</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink targetId="e90d-e5a8-f42d-da84" id="1b5b-6b8f-fb45-4c7a" primary="true" name="Allegiance:" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Brotherhood" hidden="false" id="8cf7-353a-16f4-2b4d">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="1fba-d0e9-b1ee-907d" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="f05b-d818-1457-8ae2" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="1st Brotherhood, the Swordbearers" hidden="false" id="5202-bcdf-02a3-8556" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Blades Drawn" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="b54e-eaa7-8bc1-cc27">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Assault phase). Trigger: This Advanced Reaction may be declared in the Assault phase, after an enemy unit declares a Charge against a friendly unit composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (1st) special rule, before any Overwatch attacks are resolved. Effect: The reacting unit forfeits its ability to make an Overwatch reaction against the charging unit. Instead, every model in the reacting unit gains the Counter-Attack (1) special rule until the end of the current Assault phase.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Fury of the Vanguard: Unwavering" id="08d9-75d3-0b76-8ef3" hidden="false">
                  <description>All models with the Brotherhood (1st) special rule have a Leadership Characteristic of 10 (this may not be modified above 10).</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Fury of the Vanguard: Vanguard of the Chapter" id="f827-6c38-2e93-c7bd" hidden="false">
                  <description>Models with the Brotherhood (1st) special rule gain a +1 bonus to their Attacks Characteristic in any turn in which they made a successful Charge.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="2nd Brotherhood, the Blades of Victory" hidden="false" id="6f09-ea43-f142-d3b7" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Riposte" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="bc08-0685-f23c-091a">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Assault phase). Trigger: This Advanced Reaction may be declared in the Assault phase, immediately after an enemy unit completes a successful Charge against a friendly unit composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (2nd) special rule. Effect: During the ensuing Fight sub-phase, all models in the reacting unit fight at the Initiative 10 step, regardless of their actual Initiative Characteristic or any penalties from unwieldy weapons.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Peerless Duellists: Blade Mastery" id="6751-ce5d-542d-8931" hidden="false">
                  <description>Models with the Brotherhood (2nd) special rule re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 when fighting in the Assault phase.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Peerless Duellists: Lightning Reflexes" id="b2e7-40f7-4eb7-1b93" hidden="false">
                  <description>Models with the Brotherhood (2nd) special rule gain a +1 bonus to their Initiative Characteristic.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="3rd Brotherhood, the Wardmakers" hidden="false" id="e3dc-675b-97c4-3550" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Ward of the Brotherhood" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="4863-dd64-74f0-a082">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Shooting phase). Trigger: This Advanced Reaction may be declared in the Shooting phase, after an enemy unit selects a friendly unit composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (3rd) special rule as the target of a Shooting Attack, before any To Hit rolls are made. Effect: Until the end of that Shooting Attack, all models in the reacting unit gain a 5+ Invulnerable Save. If a model already possesses an Invulnerable Save, it improves that save by +1 instead (to a maximum of 3+).</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Masters of the Aegis: Psychic Discipline" id="28ae-3244-c7ab-1f2d" hidden="false">
                  <description>Once per phase, a unit composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (3rd) special rule may re-roll a single failed Psychic check.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Masters of the Aegis: Searing Wards" id="cc19-34af-df21-a207" hidden="false">
                  <description>Any Dominus Blast or Purifying Flame psychic weapon used by a model with the Brotherhood (3rd) special rule gains the Shred special rule.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="4th Brotherhood, the Rapiers" hidden="false" id="4ea9-9fe2-fbc0-0691" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Covering Bolters" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="e915-16c3-28f4-08eb">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Shooting phase). Trigger: This Advanced Reaction may be declared in the Shooting phase, after an enemy unit selects a friendly unit composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (4th) special rule as the target of a Shooting Attack. Effect: Rather than the targeted unit reacting, a single other friendly unit composed entirely of models with the Legiones Astartes (Grey Knights) special rule within 6" of the targeted unit may immediately make a Return Fire Shooting Attack targeting the active enemy unit, following all standard Return Fire restrictions.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Precision Volley: Rapier Volleys" id="3027-cb80-4b5f-23ca" hidden="false">
                  <description>All Storm Bolters (and Combi-bolters) fired by models with the Brotherhood (4th) special rule gain the Breaching (6+) special rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Precision Volley: Steady Aim" id="89d7-7468-e5ed-deda" hidden="false">
                  <description>Models with the Brotherhood (4th) special rule re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 when making Shooting Attacks.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="5th Brotherhood, the Preservers" hidden="false" id="2e6e-bafb-e46b-2bd7" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Unyielding Anvil" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="a7b9-901e-a231-db25">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Assault phase). Trigger: This Advanced Reaction may be declared in the Assault phase, immediately after an enemy unit declares a Charge against a friendly unit composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (5th) special rule. Effect: The charging enemy unit must subtract D3 from its Charge Distance roll (to a minimum of 0).</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Bastion of Titan: Stoic Defenders" id="5e31-8755-29e9-ba7b" hidden="false">
                  <description>Models with the Brotherhood (5th) special rule gain the Feel No Pain (6+) special rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Bastion of Titan: Unbreakable" id="0119-3db3-b268-29b5" hidden="false">
                  <description>Units composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (5th) special rule automatically pass all Pinning tests.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="6th Brotherhood, the Exactors" hidden="false" id="b120-1048-c1d9-cbcf" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Swift Retribution" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="98f4-4479-9d7d-6a29">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Movement phase). Trigger: This Advanced Reaction may be declared in the Movement phase, after an enemy unit ends a move within 12" of, and within line of sight of, a friendly unit composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (6th) special rule. Effect: The reacting unit may immediately make a Shooting Attack targeting the triggering enemy unit, following all normal rules for Shooting Attacks (this counts as an Interceptor reaction).</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Inexorable Hunt: Relentless Pursuit" id="30dd-7699-a9d7-9637" hidden="false">
                  <description>Models with the Brotherhood (6th) special rule re-roll To Wound rolls of 1 against any unit containing at least one model with the Psyker Unit Sub-type, or the Daemon, Corrupted, Corrupted Engine, or Malefic Unit Type or Sub-type.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Inexorable Hunt: Sanctified Quarry" id="f337-71d6-5422-5020" hidden="false">
                  <description>Units composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (6th) special rule add +1 to their Sweeping Advance rolls.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="7th Brotherhood, the Prescient Brethren" hidden="false" id="f16c-9704-f63a-b015" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Foresight" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="13bc-80be-0ef7-d3a9">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Movement phase). Trigger: This Advanced Reaction may be declared in the Movement phase, after an enemy unit ends a move within 12" of a friendly unit composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (7th) special rule. Effect: Every model in the reacting unit may immediately make a move of up to D6 + its Initiative Characteristic in inches. This move may not bring any model within 1" of an enemy model, and does not prevent the unit from shooting or charging in its own turn.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Sight Beyond Sight: Foreseen Arrival" id="ee4b-5fc3-7e30-7b73" hidden="false">
                  <description>Add +1 to all Reserves rolls (including Deep Strike Assault rolls) made for units composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (7th) special rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Sight Beyond Sight: Perfect Teleport" id="c456-f557-c4c4-a006" hidden="false">
                  <description>Any unit composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (7th) special rule arriving via Deep Strike (or Teleport Strike) does not scatter when placed on the battlefield (it must still be placed more than 1" away from enemy models and impassable terrain).</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="8th Brotherhood, the Purifiers" hidden="false" id="fcdf-96a7-d7bc-2110" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Purging Volley" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions" hidden="false" id="502b-2a23-ac5f-b85a">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">(Assault phase). Trigger: This Advanced Reaction may be declared in the Assault phase, after an enemy unit declares a Charge against a friendly unit composed entirely of models with the Brotherhood (8th) special rule. Effect: The reacting unit makes an Overwatch Shooting Attack targeting the charging unit using the Purifying Flame psychic weapon (if equipped/known), resolving those attacks at the models' full Ballistic Skill rather than as Snap Shots.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Soul-Fire of Purity: Purifying Fire" id="73ad-3d7f-ed84-2969" hidden="false">
                  <description>Every Psyker model with the Brotherhood (8th) special rule automatically knows the Purifying Flame psychic weapon in addition to any other psychic powers or weapons it possesses.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Soul-Fire of Purity: Purity of Purpose" id="c47b-9aab-318a-1336" hidden="false">
                  <description>Models with the Brotherhood (8th) special rule gain the Hatred (Everything) special rule.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Rite of War" hidden="false" id="8c9d-79be-6114-e4ac">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="4892-bff8-3f98-89ac" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Champions of Titan" hidden="false" id="7cb9-1357-ff29-637e" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier type="set" field="242f-472e-e94f-54a6" value="0">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="10be-73fd-398d-2fdc" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="1297-a158-458c-ad5c" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="1ae5-f2f4-f0eb-de51" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="2c06-febe-9039-3348" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="2c3e-4d65-b5a4-847f" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="4870-4777-fd86-d9ab" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="4893-0eea-41c4-64f9" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="5203-ebdc-3ecd-9d1a" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="5476-ebb1-6842-9695" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="746f-72a2-ef15-55d8" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="839b-7c8d-f05b-5aff" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="8707-992d-2cb8-56c9" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="9284-11a3-8aa8-e888" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="952b-1b89-5991-8ab9" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="9cd6-4bb7-181b-67b5" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="ba09-4426-f694-81ff" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="c47e-8b19-bca1-b81c" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="d31c-4da9-5372-350c" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="e92f-9e4d-ac6b-6b2c" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="f0e1-5026-b5cf-1ffa" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="f4b5-9622-cd75-681a" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="fbe9-651b-7b02-04c1" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="242f-472e-e94f-54a6" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Effects" id="dc5b-8bca-b8fd-76b3" hidden="false">
                  <description>Any unit composed entirely of models equipped with Aegis Terminator Armour, Aegis-Cataphractii Terminator Armour, Aegis-Tartaros Terminator Armour, or any other pattern of Terminator armour that is normally selected as an Elites choice may be selected as a Troops choice in a Detachment using this Rite of War. Any unit selected as a Compulsory Troops choice in a Detachment using this Rite of War gains the Line Unit Sub-type. Any unit composed entirely of models equipped with Aegis-Cataphractii Terminator Armour (or standard Cataphractii Terminator Armour) may also be selected as a Heavy Support choice in a Detachment using this Rite of War. Any unit composed entirely of models equipped with Aegis-Tartaros Terminator Armour (or standard Tartaros Terminator Armour) may also be selected as a Fast Attack choice in a Detachment using this Rite of War.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="7642-9d1a-0b7d-ee72" hidden="false">
                  <description>Every model in a Detachment using this Rite of War must be equipped with Aegis Terminator Armour, Aegis-Cataphractii Terminator Armour, Aegis-Tartaros Terminator Armour, or another pattern of Terminator armour. Models that cannot be equipped with Terminator armour (such as standard power-armoured Infantry, Vehicles, Dreadnoughts, or Fortifications) may not be included in a Detachment using this Rite of War.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="310c-551a-e0a7-4116" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Prognosticar Vanguard" hidden="false" id="c302-c649-caa7-6507" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Effects" id="bf0f-caad-f888-aec4" hidden="false">
                  <description>Prognosticar Vanguard Squads and Watcher-in-the-Veil Squads in a Detachment using this Rite of War do not have the Support Squad special rule (allowing them to be taken as Compulsory Troops choices and score objectives). Exactor Squads may be taken as non-Compulsory Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War. A player whose army includes at least one Detachment using this Rite of War may re-roll any dice they roll to see which player takes the first turn or when attempting to Seize the Initiative.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="ada1-152a-3048-32a1" hidden="false">
                  <description>No unit in a Detachment using this Rite of War that includes any models with the Heavy Unit Sub-type may be deployed onto the battlefield during deployment, and must instead be placed into Reserves. A Detachment using this Rite of War may not select any Fortification choices. All Compulsory Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War must be Prognosticar Vanguard Squads or Watcher-in-the-Veil Squads.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="2fe1-fe48-1b83-0dbf" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Teleport Assault" hidden="false" id="237f-cee9-50aa-c5e1" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <rules>
                <rule name="Prerequisites" id="fe3f-9579-d6bb-b086" hidden="false">
                  <description>A Detachment using this Rite of War must include a Grand Master or Kaldor Draigo with the Master of the Legion special rule, and this model must be the army's Warlord.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Effects" id="ff6b-31e3-0965-9e06" hidden="false">
                  <description>Every unit in a Detachment using this Rite of War composed entirely of models with the Infantry Unit Type (including models in Aegis Power Armour, Aegis Artificer Armour, and any pattern of Aegis Terminator Armour) or the Dreadnought Unit Type (including Dreadknights) gains the Teleport Assault special rule, unless they are equipped with Jump Packs or Personal Teleporters. When taken as part of a Detachment using this Rite of War, units composed of models with the Dreadnought Unit Type may not be selected in units of more than one model.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="7aa8-f61d-7d32-1ccc" hidden="false">
                  <description>All units in a Detachment using this Rite of War with the Teleport Assault special rule must deploy by means of a Teleport Assault. A Detachment using this Rite of War may not select any Dedicated Transports or Fortification choices. Any models selected as part of a Detachment that do not have the Teleport Assault special rule (such as Vehicles, Flyers, or units with Personal Teleporters) must be placed into Reserves during deployment and may not deploy onto the battlefield at the start of the game (though units with Personal Teleporters or Deep Strike may still arrive via normal Deep Strike Assaults from Turn 2 onwards).</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="a3b3-4a7a-7444-2e86" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Purifier Crusade" hidden="false" id="0c08-5cd5-0cae-3c97" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier type="set" field="66c0-b142-b519-fcdc" value="0">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="1ae5-f2f4-f0eb-de51" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="2c3e-4d65-b5a4-847f" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="5476-ebb1-6842-9695" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="e92f-9e4d-ac6b-6b2c" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="fbe9-651b-7b02-04c1" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
                <modifier type="set" field="6cbe-db80-150c-ea22" value="0">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition type="greaterThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="7031-469a-1aeb-eab0" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="66c0-b142-b519-fcdc" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="6cbe-db80-150c-ea22" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Prerequisites" id="efab-3d2c-1762-b6ba" hidden="false">
                  <description>A Detachment using this Rite of War must include Castellan Crowe or a Brother-Captain (or a Praetor / Grand Master with the Brotherhood (8th) special rule) with the Master of the Legion special rule, and this model must be the army's Warlord.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Effects" id="70bb-d0e6-6d34-8c71" hidden="false">
                  <description>Cleansing Flame: Purifier Squads and Purifier Bladeguard Squads may be selected as Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War. Any unit selected as a Compulsory Troops choice in this manner gains the Line Unit Sub-type. March of the Incorruptible: Every unit in a Detachment using this Rite of War composed entirely of models with the Infantry Unit Type (excluding models with the Heavy Unit Sub-type) gains the Crusader special rule (adding +1 to their Run distances and Sweeping Advance rolls) and increases the range of their Purifying Flame psychic weapons by +3" (or adds +1 to the number of automatic hits inflicted by close-combat Purifying Flame / Cleansing Aura effects). Beacon of Purity: Friendly units composed entirely of models with the Legiones Astartes (Grey Knights) special rule within 12" of the army's Warlord gain the Stubborn special rule and automatically pass any Morale or Pinning tests caused by models with the Daemon, Corrupted, Corrupted Engine, or Malefic Unit Type or Sub-type. Relentless Purge: Once per game, at the start of any of the controlling player's Assault phases, the Warlord may declare a Great Cleansing. Until the end of that Assault phase, all friendly Purifier Squads and Purifier Bladeguard Squads in the Detachment gain the Rage (1) special rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="8161-6bd3-d160-b5fc" hidden="false">
                  <description>A Detachment using this Rite of War may not include any Dreadknight Talons or Dreadnought units of any type. A Detachment using this Rite of War may not include any Land Raiders or Spartan Assault Tanks of any variant (including as Dedicated Transports). A Detachment using this Rite of War may not select any Fortification choices, and may only select a single Heavy Support choice. All Compulsory Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War must be Purifier Squads or Purifier Bladeguard Squads.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="ba50-e529-ac78-ce2f" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Paladin Retinue" hidden="false" id="375b-d942-3927-3c58" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier type="set" field="33fc-ba53-daa5-97b0" value="0">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="746f-72a2-ef15-55d8" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="952b-1b89-5991-8ab9" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="f4b5-9622-cd75-681a" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
                <modifier type="set" field="7eb4-fb94-9d82-ce89" value="0">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition type="greaterThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="20ef-cd01-a8da-376e" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
                <modifier type="set" field="70e7-6132-478f-c048" value="0">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition type="greaterThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="7031-469a-1aeb-eab0" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="33fc-ba53-daa5-97b0" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="7eb4-fb94-9d82-ce89" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="70e7-6132-478f-c048" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Prerequisites" id="f1b4-11cb-e83a-d98e" hidden="false">
                  <description>A Detachment using this Rite of War must include a Grand Master or Kaldor Draigo with the Master of the Legion special rule, and this model must be the army's Warlord.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Effects" id="c6f8-bae6-36e0-7011" hidden="false">
                  <description>Chosen of the Chamber: Paladin Squads may be selected as Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War. Any unit selected as a Compulsory Troops choice in this manner gains the Line Unit Sub-type. Anvil of Titan: Every model in a Detachment using this Rite of War equipped with Aegis Terminator Armour, Aegis-Cataphractii Terminator Armour, or Aegis-Tartaros Terminator Armour gains the Stubborn and Heart of the Legion special rules (granting Feel No Pain (6+)—or improving an existing Feel No Pain roll by +1, to a maximum of 4+—while within 3" of an Objective marker). Sworn Protectors: While the army's Warlord is joined to a Paladin Squad, every model in that unit gains a +1 bonus to its Weapon Skill Characteristic when fighting in a Challenge or against units containing at least one model with the Daemon, Corrupted, Corrupted Engine, or Malefic Unit Type or Sub-type. Oath of the Inner Sanctum: Once per battle, at the start of any opposing Assault phase, the Warlord may invoke the Oath of the Inner Sanctum. Until the end of that Assault phase, all friendly Paladin Squads in the Detachment gain the Counter-Attack (1) special rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="accd-88f7-a35d-6049" hidden="false">
                  <description>A Detachment using this Rite of War may not include any Strike Squads, Interceptor Squads, or Purgation Squads. All Compulsory Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War must be Paladin Squads. A Detachment using this Rite of War may only select a single Fast Attack choice and a single Heavy Support choice, and may not select any Fortification choices.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="0cd1-795b-e397-7e85" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Nemesis Strike" hidden="false" id="4a3b-8958-41eb-9b28" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier type="set" field="ae9d-2706-6eac-8d79" value="0">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="c658-dc6b-727b-c488" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
                  </conditions>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="ae9d-2706-6eac-8d79" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Prerequisites" id="b02a-1216-a971-eb02" hidden="false">
                  <description>A Detachment using this Rite of War must include a Grand Master in Nemesis Dreadknight with the Master of the Legion special rule, and this model must be the army's Warlord.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Effects" id="89ff-12c4-64f1-c513" hidden="false">
                  <description>Engines of Tithe: Dreadknight Talons may be selected as Elites choices in addition to Heavy Support choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War. Spearhead of Titan: Grey Knight Dreadlancer Talons may be selected as non-Compulsory Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War. Any unit selected in this manner gains the Line Unit Sub-type. Resonance of the Aegis: All models with the Dreadnought Unit Type (including Dreadknight Talons and Grey Knight Dreadlancer Talons) in a Detachment using this Rite of War gain the Adamantine Will (4+) special rule (or improve an existing Adamantine Will roll by +1, to a maximum of 2+) and may re-roll failed Psychic checks when manifesting psychic weapons or powers. Sanctified Stampede: Models in a Dreadknight Talon or Grey Knight Dreadlancer Talon in a Detachment using this Rite of War gain the Hammer of Wrath (D3) special rule (resolved at the model's unmodified Strength Characteristic and AP 3) in any turn in which they make a successful Charge. Overload the Conduits: Once per battle, at the start of any of the controlling player's Shooting phases, the Warlord may trigger an Aegis Conduit Surge. Until the end of that Shooting phase, all Heavy weapons mounted on Dreadknight Talons and Grey Knight Dreadlancer Talons within 12" of the Warlord gain the Rending (6+) special rule (or improve an existing Rending value by +1, to a maximum of 4+).</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Limitations" id="ae07-680a-799d-8544" hidden="false">
                  <description>A Detachment using this Rite of War may not include any Lords of War choices. A Detachment using this Rite of War must include strictly more Troops choices than Dreadknight Talons (counted across all Force Organisation slots). A Detachment using this Rite of War may not select any Fortification choices, and may not include an Allied Detachment. All Compulsory Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War must be standard Strike Squads (or Brotherhood Terminator Squads if permitted by another rule), ensuring a core infantry support element accompanies the walker spearhead.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink targetId="d494-e450-d4aa-579a" id="7095-e817-db2a-c929" primary="true" name="Rite of War:" />
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
      </selectionEntryGroups>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
  </selectionEntries>
